A||||3||Cooter||Where to get recall information???
Z||000000||Cooter||07-01-99||08:33 PM||||I was trying to see if all the recalls and updates had been done on my car and the 1-800-PM-Cares could not help- they only have records for the past ten years. Does anybody know where you could find out about the service history of a fiero?
Z||000001||batboy||07-01-99||08:53 PM||||The local Pontiac dealership should be able to look it up on their computer for you. You will need to give them your VIN first though. That's what I did.
Z||000002||theogre||07-01-99||09:40 PM||||save yourself the time...... Call, in the US, and Canada I think, 1800PMCARES. Give them the VIN and they will gladly tell you if there are any outstanding recalls. ((For those of you buying a Fiero you should all do this.)) Recalls NEVER expire. If there are any outstanding, and a dealler refuses to do them, they are in violation of a number of laws, rules, and dealler licensing, type things. Report them to Pontiac/GM and the NTSB or NHTSA. (I think NHTSA is the right one, but I can't remember right now.  <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.dot.gov/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nhtsa.dot.gov/</A> )<p>Deallers are a pain in the ass. If the car has over 100K miles on it, Pontiac will send you a cute frame for the tag. The text of it is... top- "Over 100,000 miles of" bottom- "Pontiac Excitement- Pontiac cares" I have one. they are kind of nice, and free. they will ask for some demographic data, but in this case it's worth it. It shows GM how well these cars lasted, and how many people like them still. I strongly urge all 100K+ owners to call and get the frame even if they don't put it on the car.
Z||000003||theogre||07-01-99||09:45 PM||||the last 10 years..... I missed that. that's interesting, mine is an 87, and they seemed to have that on file. I think I'll call them again and see. Hmmmmmm.......... ((That's what happens when I don't read the whole thing I guess........ Silly Ogre. Whack¡))
